UID:17445-1789498800-1789504200@gardens.duke.edu
SUMMARY:Most Delicious Poison: A Virtual Author Talk with Noah Whiteman
DESCRIPTION:Based on cutting-edge science in the fields of evolution\, chemistry and neuroscience\, Most Delicious Poison by Noah Whiteman reveals the origins of toxins produced by plants\, mushrooms\, microbes and even some animals; the mechanisms that animals evolved to overcome them; and how a co-evolutionary arms race made its way into the human experience. This perpetual chemical war not only drove the diversification of life on Earth but is also intimately tied to our own successes and failures. You will never look at a houseplant\, mushroom\, fruit\, vegetable or even the last 500 years of human history the same way again. Offered in partnership with the Garden Forum Collaborative. \nFee: $10; free for Members of the North Carolina Botanical Garden Foundation\, Sarah P. Duke Gardens\, J.C. Raulston Arboretum\, Durham Garden Forum and Durham County Master Gardeners. Pre-registration is required for all attendees. \nRegistration: Register at go.unc.edu/whiteman \nLocation: Zoom. \nAccessibility: This will be a virtual program that takes place on Zoom with the option to enable closed captioning.
URL:https://gardens.duke.edu/event/most-delicious-poison-a-virtual-author-talk-with-noah-whiteman/
LOCATION:Virtual (Zoom)
CATEGORIES:Adult Programs,Virtual Programs
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://gardens.duke.edu/wp-content/uploads/Noah-Whiteman-Most-Delicious-Poison.jpg
END:VEVENT
