SUMMARY:Queer Ecology Family Picnic
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate PRIDE at Duke Gardens! Bring your own picnic and enjoy the outdoors as you connect with human and beyond-human queer community. Join Stormie Daie for story time. Learn about queer ecology at activity tables where you can create a creature or make a mini-zine to write\, draw and collage. Bring your own picnic blanket\, find a bench or take a stroll through the garden. This event is in collaboration with the LGBTQ Center of Durham\, as part of Durham Pride Week 2026. \nFrozen juice pops will be available while supplies last\, plus a limited amount of pizza donated by Pride Sponsor Pie Pushers for anyone unable to bring your own picnic. \nThis event is for all ages; come on your own or with family & friends. Rain or shine! If it rains\, the same activities will move inside the Doris Duke Center for an indoor picnic. \nFee: Free; no registration required. \nParking: Free parking provided in Duke Gardens’ main parking lot. \nLocation: Gateway Gardens Event Lawn \nAccessibility: This event takes place outdoors and requires traveling on a combination of gently sloping paved paths and grass lawns. Accessible parking and bathrooms are available onsite.
URL:https://gardens.duke.edu/event/queer-ecology-family-picnic/
LOCATION:Gateway Gardens Event Lawn
END:VEVENT
