SUMMARY:Mixed-Media Floral Greeting Cards
DESCRIPTION:In this guided mixed-media workshop with Patricia Efunsade\, founder and creative director of SaKredJoi Art\, participants will create a series of botanically inspired greeting cards using a simple and approachable collage process. Begin by creating an 8.5 x 11-inch collage master sheet—a mixed-media process rooted in experimentation\, layering\, composition and storytelling through paper. Participants will then transform the paper into four unique handmade cards with designs that feature hand-cut flowers\, stems and leaves. Everyone will complete four finished greeting cards\, with the option to add personal words or sentiments. \nThis workshop is designed to be both relaxing and creatively engaging\, with a clear process that allows participants of all experience levels to leave with finished work that is ready to send or frame. All materials provided. \nFee: $45; 20% discount for Duke Gardens members with discount code. \nParking: Parking fees apply. \nLocation: Pelham-Cullen Classroom inside the Barnes Welcome Center. \nAccessibility: This program takes place seated in an indoor location accessible via paved surfaces and equipped with a hearing loop\, which transmits sound directly to hearing aids and cochlear implants with a T-coil setting. Accessible restrooms are available onsite.
URL:https://gardens.duke.edu/event/mixed-media-floral-greeting-cards/
LOCATION:Duke Gardens–Pelham-Cullen Classroom in the Barnes Welcome Center\, 420 Anderson Street\, Durham\, NC\, 27705\, United States
